The seven non-empty subsets of \{R,G,B\} are equally likely, each with prior probability \(1/7\).  
Given a subset of size \(k\), each marble in the bag is drawn with probability \(1/k\) (sampling with replacement), so the likelihood of the sequence R, B, R is:

- Subsets missing R or missing B: likelihood \(0\).
- \(\{R,B\}\) (\(k=2\)): \((\tfrac12)^3 = \tfrac18\).
- \(\{R,G,B\}\) (\(k=3\)): \((\tfrac13)^3 = \tfrac1{27}\).

Thus
\[
P(\{R,B\}\mid \text{data})=\frac{\frac18\cdot\frac17}{\frac18\cdot\frac17+\frac1{27}\cdot\frac17}
=\frac{\frac18}{\frac18+\frac1{27}}
=\frac{27}{27+8}
=\frac{27}{35}.
\]

